{"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/GLib\/documentation\/GLib","doc:\/\/GLib\/documentation\/GLib\/Variant","doc:\/\/GLib\/documentation\/GLib\/Variant\/VariantProtocol-Implementations"]]},"kind":"symbol","variants":[{"paths":["\/documentation\/glib\/variant\/takeref()"],"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}]}],"sections":[],"schemaVersion":{"minor":3,"major":0,"patch":0},"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"If "},{"code":"value","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" is floating, sink it.  Otherwise, do nothing."}],"primaryContentSections":[{"declarations":[{"languages":["swift"],"tokens":[{"text":"func","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"takeRef","kind":"identifier"},{"text":"() -> ","kind":"text"},{"text":"VariantRef","preciseIdentifier":"s:4GLib10VariantRefV","identifier":"doc:\/\/GLib\/documentation\/GLib\/VariantRef","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":"!","kind":"text"}],"platforms":["macOS"]}],"kind":"declarations"},{"content":[{"type":"heading","anchor":"discussion","text":"Discussion","level":2},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Typically you want to use ","type":"text"},{"code":"g_variant_ref_sink()","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" in order to","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"automatically do the correct thing with respect to floating or","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"non-floating references, but there is one specific scenario where"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":"this function is helpful."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The situation where this function is helpful is when creating an API"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"text":"that allows the user to provide a callback function that returns a","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/GLib\/documentation\/GLib\/Variant"},{"type":"text","text":".  We certainly want to allow the user the flexibility to"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"return a non-floating reference from this callback (for the case"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":"where the value that is being returned already exists)."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"At the same time, the style of the "},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/GLib\/documentation\/GLib\/Variant"},{"type":"text","text":" API makes it likely that"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"text":"for newly-created ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/GLib\/documentation\/GLib\/Variant","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" instances, the user can be saved some"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"typing if they are allowed to return a "},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/GLib\/documentation\/GLib\/Variant"},{"text":" with a floating","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"text":"reference.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Using this function on the return value of the user’s callback allows"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"the user to do whichever is more convenient for them.  The caller","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"will always receives exactly one full reference to the value: either"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"text":"the one that was returned in the first place, or a floating reference","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":"that has been converted to a full reference."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"This function has an odd interaction when combined with","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"code":"g_variant_ref_sink()","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" running at the same time in another thread on"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":"the same "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/GLib\/documentation\/GLib\/Variant","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":" instance.  If ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"g_variant_ref_sink()"},{"type":"text","text":" runs first then"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"text":"the result will be that the floating reference is converted to a hard","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":"reference.  If "},{"code":"g_variant_take_ref()","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" runs first then the result will","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"be that the floating reference is converted to a hard reference and"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":"an additional reference on top of that one is added.  It is best to"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"avoid this situation."}]}],"kind":"content"}],"metadata":{"symbolKind":"method","title":"takeRef()","extendedModule":"GLib","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"func"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"kind":"identifier","text":"takeRef"},{"kind":"text","text":"() -> "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:4GLib10VariantRefV","text":"VariantRef"},{"kind":"text","text":"!"}],"modules":[{"name":"GLib"}],"externalID":"s:4GLib15VariantProtocolPAAE7takeRefAA0bE0VSgyF::SYNTHESIZED::s:4GLib7VariantC","role":"symbol","roleHeading":"Instance Method"},"identifier":{"interfaceLanguage":"swift","url":"doc:\/\/GLib\/documentation\/GLib\/Variant\/takeRef()"},"references":{"doc://GLib/documentation/GLib/Variant":{"role":"symbol","kind":"symbol","navigatorTitle":[{"text":"Variant","kind":"identifier"}],"title":"Variant","identifier":"doc:\/\/GLib\/documentation\/GLib\/Variant","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"class"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Variant","kind":"identifier"}],"abstract":[{"code":"GVariant","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" is a variant datatype; it can contain one or more values"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"along with information about the type of the values."}],"type":"topic","url":"\/documentation\/glib\